NAME
       getdents, readdir - read directory entries

SYNOPSIS
       #include <dirent.h>

       DIR           *opendir(const char *path);
       struct dirent *readdir(DIR *d);
       int            closedir(DIR *d);

DESCRIPTION
       Walks a directory. Each entry carries d_name and d_type, where
       d_type distinguishes a directory from a regular file without a
       separate stat, which matters when listing a large tree.

       getdents is the underlying syscall and fills a caller-supplied
       buffer with several entries at a time.

RETURN VALUE
       readdir returns an entry, or NULL at the end of the directory or
       on error.

ERRORS
       ENOENT    the directory does not exist
       ENOTDIR   the path is not a directory

SEE ALSO
       stat(2), ls(1), find(1)
